 "final_message": "Brightpath issued a Loan Estimate, but the rate is above Sam and Nadia's limit, so I did not record intent to proceed.\n\n**What I did**\n- **Documents gathered:** I downloaded the last 2 monthly statements for each of the four personal accounts: Sam's Juniper checking and savings, and Nadia's Northgate checking and savings. I also downloaded the last 2 Larkspur General Hospital payslips for each of them. I did not touch Nadia's business account.\n- **Application:** I filled in the borrower, employment and income, assets, and property and loan sections. The loan is $440,000, 30-year fixed, on 14 Larch Lane. I uploaded those 12 documents, gave the credit-check and e-sign consents, and submitted once. The application number is **BHL-26001**.\n- **Underwriting condition:** Brightpath asked about an $8,000 mobile check deposit on 09/03/2026 into Sam's checking account ending 4417. Sam and Nadia told me it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment, not a loan. I sent that as the written response and the lender confirmed receipt.\n\n**Loan Estimate (LE-BHL-26001-1)**\n\n| Item | Estimate | Your limit | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Interest rate | **6.875%** | at most 6.5% | **Over** |\n| Monthly payment | $2,890.49 | at most $3,100 | OK |\n| Closing costs | $12,850 | at most $14,000 | OK |\n\nThe APR is 7.041%, and the lender says a rate lock is available for 45 days. The estimate shows $0 for taxes and insurance (escrow), so the real monthly payment may be higher once those are added.\n\n**Status:** the application is submitted and under conditional review. Sam and Nadia will need to decide whether to ask Brightpath for a lower rate, shop other lenders, or change their limits.",
